  </div></div></div>
<div class="sc-pillars-band" data-hana-bg="wafer" data-variant="light" data-accent="" data-fade="none" style="background:linear-gradient(120deg,#f5f7fa 35%,#d8e6f3 100%);position:relative;overflow:hidden;"><div class="cap-section cap-section--band"><div style="margin-bottom:64px;"><div style="margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0;">Capability overview</h2><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:15.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;max-width:640px;margin:10px 0 0;">From discretes to modules, the package architecture, interconnect, and thermal path support the electrical and thermal requirements of the device.</p></div><div class="cap-grid-3"><div class="sc-pillar" style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);overflow:hidden;background:#fff;display:flex;flex-direction:column;"><div style="padding:22px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;flex:1;"><div style="width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:8px;background:var(--hana-blue);color:#fff;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:14px;"><i data-lucide="cpu" style="width:18px;height:18px;"></i></div><div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:20px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);letter-spacing:-0.01em;margin-bottom:10px;">Power discretes</div><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;margin:0 0 16px;">Production-ready high-power discrete formats.</p><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0 0 16px;"><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">TO-247 in 2L, 3L and 4L</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">D2PAK-7L</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">TOLL</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">SiC diodes and MOSFETs, SJ MOS, and FRFET</span></li></ul></div></div><div class="sc-pillar" style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);overflow:hidden;background:#fff;display:flex;flex-direction:column;"><div style="padding:22px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;flex:1;"><div style="width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:8px;background:var(--hana-blue);color:#fff;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:14px;"><i data-lucide="box" style="width:18px;height:18px;"></i></div><div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:20px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);letter-spacing:-0.01em;margin-bottom:10px;">Power modules</div><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;margin:0 0 16px;">Established module footprints for high-power applications.</p><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0 0 16px;"><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">34 mm, 62 mm and XM3</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">EconoDual 3, Econo and PIM</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">HP1 and Easy 1B / 2B / 3B</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Custom SiP assembly with SiC on DBC</span></li></ul></div></div><div class="sc-pillar" style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);overflow:hidden;background:#fff;display:flex;flex-direction:column;"><div style="padding:22px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;flex:1;"><div style="width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:8px;background:var(--hana-blue);color:#fff;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;margin-bottom:14px;"><i data-lucide="thermometer" style="width:18px;height:18px;"></i></div><div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:20px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);letter-spacing:-0.01em;margin-bottom:10px;">Thermal &amp; interconnect</div><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.55;margin:0 0 16px;">Thermal and interconnect choices that protect the device rating.</p><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0 0 16px;"><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Copper-clip interconnect in place of source wire bonds</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Dual-cool construction on PDFN 8×8, PLP 8×8, and TO-247TE</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Ceramic DBC substrates for electrical isolation</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:8px;align-items:baseline;padding:6px 0;"><span style="color:var(--hana-blue);font-weight:700;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.5;">Vacuum reflow to control thermal-path voiding</span></li></ul></div></div></div></div></div></div>
<div style="background:#fff;"><div class="cap-section"><div style="margin-bottom:44px;"><div class="why-grid why-grid--single"><div style="position:relative;overflow:hidden;border-radius:var(--radius-panel);padding:32px 30px;background:linear-gradient(152deg,#155F9B 0%,#0E4A7C 46%,#0A3860 100%);border:none;"><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;margin-bottom:18px;"><img src="/images/hana-mark-white.svg" alt="" style="width:36px;height:36px;display:block;flex:none;"><span style="flex:1;height:1px;background:rgba(255,255,255,0.24);"></span></div><h3 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:23px;font-weight:600;color:#fff;line-height:1.22;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0 0 12px;text-wrap:balance;">Interconnect and package construction designed for high-current devices</h3><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:14.5px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.84);line-height:1.6;margin:0 0 16px;">Copper-clip interconnect reduces source-path resistance and supports higher current within the package outline. Dual-cool constructions provide thermal paths through both sides of the package, while vacuum reflow helps control voiding through the thermal interface.</p><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0;margin:0;"><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);"><span style="color:#7EC8FF;font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.88);line-height:1.55;">Higher current capability in the same footprint</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);"><span style="color:#7EC8FF;font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.88);line-height:1.55;">Support for higher device ratings within established package outlines</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);"><span style="color:#7EC8FF;font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.88);line-height:1.55;">Lower source-connection resistance</span></li><li style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:16px 1fr;gap:10px;align-items:baseline;padding:9px 0;border-top:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.2);"><span style="color:#7EC8FF;font-size:14px;font-weight:700;line-height:1;">&rsaquo;</span><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;color:rgba(255,255,255,0.88);line-height:1.55;">A more consistent thermal path through controlled voiding</span></li></ul></div></div></div></div></div>
<div style="background:var(--hana-blue-tint);"><div class="cap-section"><div style="margin-bottom:8px;"><div style="margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0;">Where we run it</h2><p style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:15.5px;color:var(--ink-2);line-height:1.6;max-width:640px;margin:10px 0 0;">Power package assembly is available across our OSAT network; production mix varies by site.</p></div><div class="cap-grid-4"><a href="/locations/ayutthaya" style="text-decoration:none;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);padding:22px;background:#fff;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;"><div><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;margin-bottom:7px;"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:14px;height:14px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:11px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.08em;color:var(--hana-blue);">Thailand</span></div><div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:22px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink);letter-spacing:-0.01em;">Ayutthaya</div></div><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hana-blue);">Explore Ayutthaya <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--hana-blue)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span></a><a href="/locations/jiaxing" style="text-decoration:none;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);padding:22px;background:#fff;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px;"><div><div style="display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;margin-bottom:7px;"><i data-lucide="map-pin" style="width:14px;height:14px;color:var(--hana-blue);"></i><span style="font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:11px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.08em;color:var(--hana-blue);">China</span></div><div style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:22px;font-weight:700;color:var(--ink);letter-spacing:-0.01em;">Jiaxing</div></div><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;font-family:var(--font-text);font-size:13.5px;font-weight:600;color:var(--hana-blue);">Explore Jiaxing <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--hana-blue)" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M5 12h14"></path><path d="m12 5 7 7-7 7"></path></svg></span></a></div></div></div></div>
<div style="background:#fff;"><div class="cap-section"><div style="margin-bottom:8px;"><div style="margin-bottom:26px;"><h2 style="font-family:var(--font-display);font-size:28px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink);line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0;">Frequently asked questions</h2></div><div style="border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:var(--radius-card);overflow:hidden;background:#fff;"><details class="sc-faq" open><summary>Which module formats do you assemble?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary><div class="sc-faq-a">34 mm, 62 mm, XM3, EconoDual 3, Econo, PIM, HP1 and Easy 1B, 2B and 3B — plus SiC on DBC built into a custom SiP where a standard format does not fit.</div></details><details class="sc-faq"><summary>How do you manage thermal performance in a wide-bandgap package?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary><div class="sc-faq-a">Copper clip interconnect instead of wire bonds, dual-cooled pads exposed top and bottom, and ceramic DBC substrates. Voids in the thermal path are held under 5% by vacuum reflow.</div></details><details class="sc-faq"><summary>What voltage and isolation class can you assemble to?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary><div class="sc-faq-a">Devices to the 1200 V class, with built-in isolation above 2500 V on the TO-247TE outline.</div></details><details class="sc-faq"><summary>What is this used for?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary><div class="sc-faq-a">EV and hybrid drivetrains, rail traction, solar and wind inverters, industrial drives, and data center power.</div></details><details class="sc-faq"><summary>Can you build a module footprint that isn't one of the standards?<span class="sc-faq-mk">+</span></summary><div class="sc-faq-a">Yes — SiC on DBC assembled into a custom SiP. If the outline itself has to be drawn, that runs through package design and simulation before any tooling is cut.</div></details></div></div></div></div>
<div style="background:#fff;"><div class="cap-section"><div data-hana-bg="pcb" data-variant="dark" data-accent="" data-fade="none" style="margin:0 0 64px;padding:30px 34px;border-radius:var(--radius-panel);background:var(--hana-blue-deep);color:#fff;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:28px;flex-wrap:wrap;position:relative;overflow:hidden;">
